{
 "as_of": "2026-10-05",
 "descriptor": "Defence simulators and anti-drone systems",
 "lede": "India's leading maker of combat simulators and anti-drone systems, with high margins, ₹1,200 Cr of cash and big ambitions. Orders have dried up while management keeps promising ₹4,000 Cr of revenue over two years, and 40% of purchases go to a company linked to the MD.",
 "market": {
  "price": 1576,
  "mcap_cr": 14231,
  "pe": 78.3,
  "pb": 7.5,
  "ev_ebitda": 59
 },
 "short_version": [
  {
   "lead": "What's going right",
   "text": "Proven products (anti-drone systems used in Operation Sindoor, tank and gunnery simulators), 30%+ net margins, debt-free with about ₹1,217 Cr of cash, and a ₹177.5 Cr MoD order after Q1."
  },
  {
   "lead": "What to be sceptical about",
   "text": "FY26 revenue fell 29% to ₹688 Cr; Q1 FY27 orders were only ₹44.6 Cr and the order book shrank to ₹1,239 Cr. The ₹4,000 Cr two-year revenue target needs revenue to triple. About 40% of purchases are from related parties, mainly Unistring Tech, where the MD is a director."
  },
  {
   "lead": "Price",
   "text": "78x trailing earnings (about 59x EV/EBITDA net of cash), on par with Data Patterns (88x) and below Paras (110x), but with falling revenue."
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "business",
   "title": "Company overview and business model",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Zen designs combat training simulators (tank, gunnery, naval, flight) and anti-drone systems, and is adding interceptor drones, unmanned ground vehicles, remote weapon stations, smart ammunition and a cyber-security suite. Customers are the Indian armed forces, MoD and friendly foreign governments; subsidiaries ARI and UTS add naval and other simulators.",
     "src": "May call p.2"
    },
    {
     "type": "tiles",
     "items": [
      {
       "value": "₹1,239 Cr",
       "label": "Order book, Jun 2026 (₹921 Cr equipment, ₹318 Cr AMC)"
      },
      {
       "value": "72.9%",
       "label": "Gross margin, Q1 FY27"
      },
      {
       "value": "~₹1,217 Cr",
       "label": "Cash, debt-free"
      },
      {
       "value": "₹365 Cr",
       "label": "Subsidiaries' FY27 revenue target"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "Where the profit comes from",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Gross margins above 70% on in-house designed products; most hardware is outsourced and assembled.",
       "src": "Jul call p.3"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "A large fixed cost base: margins swing with revenue (27% EBITDA in Q1 FY27 vs 41% a year earlier).",
       "src": "Jul call p.3"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Annual maintenance contracts (AMC) give years of follow-on revenue after delivery.",
       "src": "Jul call p.16"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "What changed in 3–5 years",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Revenue went from ₹70 Cr (FY22) to ₹974 Cr (FY25) on large anti-drone orders, then fell to ₹688 Cr.",
       "src": null
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Raised about ₹1,000 Cr through a QIP in FY25; acquired ARI and others.",
       "src": null
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Arms and ammunition licences received; expanding into weapon systems.",
       "src": "May call p.14"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
